[Jet]
Hey little guy, hope I didn't keep you waiting long.

[Pizza]
Maooww

[Jet]
Yeah, I know, I know, I'm sorry. C'mere, let's get you all dried up and warm.

[Narrator]
You pat the cat with your towel cautiously and awkwardly at first. Pizza's eyes narrow and his ears flatten a little at the clumsy dabbing.

[Narrator]
Sensing your hesitation, he nuzzles against your hand and turns this way and that to make drying him easier.

[Pizza]
Purrrr... prrr... mrrr

[Jet]
Aww, there we go, that's better! Look at you, you're all fluffy and warm now, right, Pizza?

[Narrator]
As the word 'Pizza' leaves your mouth, your stomach begins to growl and gurgle, startling the poor furball.

[Jet]
Sorry, it's been a while since I last ate...

[Narrator]
A second, much lower rumbling noise sounds out, this time from Pizza himself.

[Pizza]
Grrrrmmm.

[Jet]
You too, huh? How about I scrounge us up something tasty to eat from the kitchen?

[Pizza]
Miau!

[Jet]
Yeah? You'd like that? Just don't get your hopes up, little guy. The pantry's been looking pretty bleak lately.{setprogress 4}